{"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Send records to an Amplitude project through its HTTP V2 API."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/amplitude(apiKey:region:plan:backoff:clock:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" makes an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (module ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations","type":"reference"},{"text":") for your Amplitude project in one call. It checks","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the API key, posts to the HTTP V2 endpoint of the project’s data residency (","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeRegion","type":"reference"},{"text":")","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with an ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeBatchEncoder","type":"reference"},{"text":", and splits each batch to Amplitude’s limits","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeBatchEncoder\/batchLimit","type":"reference"},{"text":"): 10 events and 1 MB a request, which a project on any plan","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"accepts. A batch with no record the encoder can write, an empty one included, makes no request. It","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"retries no response, a 5xx, 408 and 429, and drops and reports any other status. The API key goes","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"in the body, so no header field is needed, and no trace context is sent. ","type":"text"},{"code":"import Traffluent","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"leaves this module out; import it on its own.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The region has no default. A project’s data resides in Amplitude’s default data center or its EU","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"one, and an event posted to the other doesn’t reach it, so you pick the region on purpose. The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"factory throws ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeSetupError","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" for an empty key, and for an Amplitude Experiment deployment","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"key, which isn’t the project’s API key.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each record becomes an event of an anonymous device. Its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"device_id"},{"type":"text","text":" is the record’s session,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from the sessions enricher, and its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"session_id"},{"type":"text","text":" that session’s start in Unix milliseconds; a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"record with no session is sent under its own record identifier, with no "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"session_id"},{"type":"text","text":". No "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"user_id"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is sent. Its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"insert_id"},{"type":"text","text":" is the record’s identifier, which a redelivered record keeps, and its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"time"},{"type":"text","text":" the record’s timestamp in epoch milliseconds. The record’s vendor identifier and trace"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"context aren’t sent, nor is an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ip"},{"type":"text","text":", and the standard context is sent as Amplitude’s own fields"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"app_version"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"device_model"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"language"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"platform"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"os_name"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"os_version"},{"type":"text","text":")."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Amplitude counts a user per ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"device_id"},{"text":" and bills by monthly tracked users, so each session counts","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"as one tracked user, and so does each record sent without a session.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Properties are read through the event’s schema in the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TrackingPlan"},{"type":"text","text":" the encoder is made with, into"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"event_properties"},{"type":"text","text":". A "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sensitive"},{"type":"text","text":" value is never sent, whatever the record reveals. A record the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"encoder can’t write is left out and the rest of the batch is sent: one the plan doesn’t describe,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one whose event name Amplitude keeps for its own ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"[Amplitude] …"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$identify"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$groupidentify"},{"type":"text","text":"),"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one whose event isn’t "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Encodable"},{"type":"text","text":", one holding a value JSON can’t, one whose timestamp has no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"epoch-milliseconds form, and one too large for a request. The destination reports each as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDropReport.skipped(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SkippedRecord"},{"type":"text","text":" whose reason is an "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeEncodingError","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"To send to PostHog, use ","type":"text"},{"code":"PostHogEncoding","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" instead.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["import AmplitudeEncoding","import HTTPDestinations","import TrackingPlans","","let plan = try TrackingPlan()","let amplitude = try HTTPDestination.amplitude(","    apiKey: apiKey,","    region: .us,  \/\/ or .eu, where the project's data resides","    plan: plan)","let tracker = Tracker(enrichers: [.sessions()])","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: amplitude)"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The guide "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"covers what Amplitude receives, and why, in more detail."}]}]}],"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/amplitudeencoding"]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"metadata":{"role":"collection","modules":[{"name":"AmplitudeEncoding"}],"roleHeading":"Framework","title":"AmplitudeEncoding","externalID":"AmplitudeEncoding","symbolKind":"module"},"topicSections":[{"title":"Sending to Amplitude","anchor":"Sending-to-Amplitude","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/amplitude(apiKey:region:plan:backoff:clock:)","doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/amplitude(apiKey:region:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)","doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeRegion","doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeSetupError"]},{"title":"Encoding batches","anchor":"Encoding-batches","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeBatchEncoder"]},{"title":"Records left out","anchor":"Records-left-out","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeEncodingError"]}],"references":{"https://tyler-keith-thompson.github.io/Traffluent/documentation/traffluent/choosingdestinations":{"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations","url":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations","titleInlineContent":[{"text":"Choosing Destinations","type":"text"}],"type":"link","title":"Choosing Destinations"},"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations/BatchEncoder":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"What turns a batch of records into the requests "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" sends."}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"BatchEncoder"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"BatchEncoder"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations\/batchencoder","title":"BatchEncoder","role":"symbol"},"doc://AmplitudeEncoding/documentation/AmplitudeEncoding/AmplitudeBatchEncoder":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder"},{"type":"text","text":" of Amplitude’s HTTP V2 API, so an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" can"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"send events to an Amplitude project’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"POST \/2\/httpapi"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"url":"\/documentation\/amplitudeencoding\/amplitudebatchencoder","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"AmplitudeBatchEncoder","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeBatchEncoder","title":"AmplitudeBatchEncoder","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AmplitudeBatchEncoder","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://AmplitudeEncoding/documentation/AmplitudeEncoding/AmplitudeEncodingError":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Why "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeBatchEncoder"},{"type":"text","text":" couldn’t send a record, which it leaves out of the batch’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"requests as a "},{"code":"SkippedRecord","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" reports as a drop. When it can encode no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"record of a batch, it makes no request, and "},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" sends nothing for the batch."}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"AmplitudeEncodingError"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"AmplitudeEncodingError"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeEncodingError","title":"AmplitudeEncodingError","url":"\/documentation\/amplitudeencoding\/amplitudeencodingerror","type":"topic","role":"symbol"},"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations":{"url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Send each batch of records to an HTTP endpoint, and send it again until it arrives."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations","type":"topic","role":"collection","title":"HTTPDestinations","kind":"symbol"},"doc://AmplitudeEncoding/documentation/AmplitudeEncoding":{"abstract":[{"text":"Send records to an Amplitude project through its HTTP V2 API.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/amplitudeencoding","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding","title":"AmplitudeEncoding","role":"collection"},"doc://AmplitudeEncoding/documentation/AmplitudeEncoding/AmplitudeSetupError":{"type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"AmplitudeSetupError"}],"url":"\/documentation\/amplitudeencoding\/amplitudesetuperror","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"AmplitudeSetupError"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeSetupError","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Why "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/amplitude(apiKey:region:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"couldn’t make a destination."}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"AmplitudeSetupError"},"doc://AmplitudeEncoding/documentation/AmplitudeEncoding/AmplitudeRegion":{"title":"AmplitudeRegion","identifier":"doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeRegion","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"AmplitudeRegion"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The data center an Amplitude project’s data resides in, which decides the HTTP V2 endpoint its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"events are posted to."}],"role":"symbol","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"AmplitudeRegion"}],"url":"\/documentation\/amplitudeencoding\/amplituderegion"},"doc://AmplitudeEncoding/documentation/AmplitudeEncoding/HTTPDestinations/HTTPDestination/amplitude(apiKey:region:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)":{"title":"amplitude(apiKey:region:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/amplitude(apiKey:region:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)","fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"amplitude","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"apiKey","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"region","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AmplitudeRegion","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:17AmplitudeEncoding0A6RegionO"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"plan","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"TrackingPlan","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:13TrackingPlans0A4PlanV"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"transport","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Transport","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"backoff","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ExponentialBackoff","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations18Expon